    "notes": "Side A extraction faithfully reflects the source: point estimate OR 0.55 (direction '-' for the point estimate) with assertion 'not_confirmed', matching 'but not in postmenopausal women with obesity (OR 0.55, 95% CI 0.27-1.14)' and the conclusion that high adiponectin showed no inverse association in this subgroup. Side B extraction is also faithful: the abstract reports only that adiponectin was 'independently associated with the metabolic syndrome' (p = 0.020) on multivariate logistic regression and never states the direction of the estimate, so estimate_direction null is correct. The obstacle to comparison is not an extraction error but missing essential information on side B."
